I posted this as "[PATCH] src/lab-process-mail: Name the three sources
of work" [1]. It adds a Sources section to prompt.md that lists the
three branches from most settled to least. It tells the agent to
consult all three, to rely on each only as far as it is settled, and
to prefer what is already on the base, since the aim is a series
accepted as first posted.

I put it in the prompt rather than the script because the script has
nothing to do with the sources yet. It only needs the base, which
LAB_BASE_BRANCH already provides. If you would rather have the three
named as settings too, e.g. LAB_SOURCES, I can do that. For now I
would leave them out, since a setting nothing reads is just noise.

> Also, there's thinking about input / output channels. Essentially right
